            <profile id="081f-2465-f96a-53e7" name="Equipment and options (as printed in WAB2 army list)" publicationId="15ea-5299-d0f5-5dbb" hidden="false" typeId="b19e-ee0c-17d1-6e33" typeName="Equipment and Notes">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Text" typeId="63ac-8f60-d28a-2232">Hand weapon. Rides a horse. May have light armour (+3 pts) or heavy armour (+4 pts), bow (+3 pts), javelins (+2 pts), and either thrusting or throwing spear &amp; shield (+4 pts), or kontos &amp; buckler (+4 pts). May have barding (+4 pts). Characters leading a unit of dismounted cavalry may dismount (-8 pts, reduce Movement to 4). Heraclian characters may exchange kontos &amp; buckler for Kontarion &amp; shield (+1 pt) and may have half-barding for their mounts (+2 pts). Magisters and Emperors may ride warhorses (+8 pts). The Magister is the Army General. 0-1. Justinian or Heraclian armies led by a Magister may use the Stratagem special rule; in Heraclian armies exceeding 2,000 pts one Magister may be upgraded to Basileus (Emperor, +25 pts, Leadership 10) who becomes the Army General. (Byzantium p.38)</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
            <profile id="d163-2fdd-49ab-09be" name="Armour Save" hidden="false" typeId="0dbe-f4ed-ef08-8e86" typeName="Armour Save">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Save" typeId="603e-2898-6af9-6cf1">None</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="With conditional bonuses" typeId="5882-dd5a-bc28-4024">-</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="Notes" typeId="d5e4-804e-6192-0114">Armour save from armour, shield and barding bonus pips (rulebook pp.95-98); maximum 3+ (2+ for barded cavalry). M already includes encumbrance for armour/barding (p.96). Conditional pips are in the next column.</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
              <modifiers>
                <!-- armour-save -->
