            <profile id="59e8-d302-caf2-3f5e" name="Equipment and options (as printed in WAB2 army list)" publicationId="15ea-5299-d0f5-5dbb" hidden="false" typeId="b19e-ee0c-17d1-6e33" typeName="Equipment and Notes">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Text" typeId="63ac-8f60-d28a-2232">Hand weapon, light armour, Kontarion and shield. May have heavy armour (+1 pt). The Bucellarii may also take bows (+2 pts), and either half-barding (+2 pts) or barding (+4 pts) for their mounts. Dismounted Cavalry Option: may dismount (-10 pts, reduce Movement to 4). Defensores &amp; Cursores: for every two units of the same type and with the same equipment, the smallest unit may be designated as Cursores (free), who count as light cavalry. Combined Formation - up to a third of the models in any unit may exchange Kontarion for either javelins (-1 pt) or bow (free) - archers/javelineers are placed in the rear ranks. Mounted cavalrymen are Superior Byzantine Cavalry. Dismounted cavalrymen may form a shieldwall. The Bucellarii and Optimates may be Drilled (+1 pt). The Bucellarii must be the smallest cavalry unit in the army, cannot be fielded as Cursores, and must be led by the Army General at all times. 0-1 unit. When led by the Emperor the Bucellarii may be upgraded to Excubitores (+4 pts per model) who wield maces (treat as hand weapons), have heavy armour, a shield and ride barded horses. (Byzantium p.39)</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
            <profile id="0446-0296-91f3-46f9" name="Armour Save" hidden="false" typeId="0dbe-f4ed-ef08-8e86" typeName="Armour Save">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Save" typeId="603e-2898-6af9-6cf1">4+</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="With conditional bonuses" typeId="5882-dd5a-bc28-4024">-</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="Notes" typeId="d5e4-804e-6192-0114">Armour save from armour, shield and barding bonus pips (rulebook pp.95-98); maximum 3+ (2+ for barded cavalry). M already includes encumbrance for armour/barding (p.96). Conditional pips are in the next column.</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
              <modifiers>
                <!-- armour-save -->
              <modifier type="set" field="603e-2898-6af9-6cf1" value="3+">
                <conditions>
                <condition field="selections" scope="622e-b2f9-8ced-4023" value="1" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false" childId="e94c-8e8e-ad4f-dc25" type="atLeast"/>
                <condition field="selections" scope="622e-b2f9-8ced-4023" value="1" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false" childId="127c-9f10-5c65-1425" type="lessThan"/>
                </conditions>
              </modifier>
              <modifier type="set" field="603e-2898-6af9-6cf1" value="3+">
                <conditions>
                <condition field="selections" scope="622e-b2f9-8ced-4023" value="1" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false" childId="e94c-8e8e-ad4f-dc25" type="lessThan"/>
                <condition field="selections" scope="622e-b2f9-8ced-4023" value="1" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false" childId="127c-9f10-5c65-1425" type="atLeast"/>
                </conditions>
              </modifier>
              <modifier type="set" field="603e-2898-6af9-6cf1" value="2+">
                <conditions>
                <condition field="selections" scope="622e-b2f9-8ced-4023" value="1" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false" childId="e94c-8e8e-ad4f-dc25" type="atLeast"/>
                <condition field="selections" scope="622e-b2f9-8ced-4023" value="1" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false" childId="127c-9f10-5c65-1425" type="atLeast"/>
                </conditions>
              </modifier>
              </modifiers>
            </profile>
          </profiles>
          <infoLinks>
