            </profile>
            <profile id="0cd3-b6d2-f2a6-275d" name="Equipment and options (as printed in WAB2 army list)" publicationId="15ea-5299-d0f5-5dbb" hidden="false" typeId="b19e-ee0c-17d1-6e33" typeName="Equipment and Notes">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Text" typeId="63ac-8f60-d28a-2232">Hand weapon, bow, light armour and kontos. May have buckler (+1 pt), and heavy armour instead of light armour (+1 pt). May dismount (-12 pts, reduce Movement to 4); dismounted Nobles may have shield (+2 pts). Mounted Nobles are treated as Superior Byzantine Cavalry. For every Noble model, at least one Horse Archer model must be taken as well (not enforced). Part of the 0-2 Huns allowance (0-1 Nobles). (Byzantium p.41)</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
            <profile id="3b96-2322-abad-d358" name="Armour Save" hidden="false" typeId="0dbe-f4ed-ef08-8e86" typeName="Armour Save">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Save" typeId="603e-2898-6af9-6cf1">6+</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="With conditional bonuses" typeId="5882-dd5a-bc28-4024">-</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="Notes" typeId="d5e4-804e-6192-0114">Armour save from armour, shield and barding bonus pips (rulebook pp.95-98); maximum 3+ (2+ for barded cavalry). M already includes encumbrance for armour/barding (p.96). Conditional pips are in the next column.</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
              <modifiers>
                <!-- armour-save -->
              <modifier type="set" field="5882-dd5a-bc28-4024" value="5+ with Buckler +1 in hand-to-hand only">
