  <sharedRules>
    <rule id="719f-4dda-8d6c-b96f" name="Early Byzantines (Byzantium) - List Notes" publicationId="15ea-5299-d0f5-5dbb" hidden="false">
      <description>EARLY BYZANTINES (Byzantium: Beyond the Golden Gate, pp.34-43). Allies and Mercenaries (Symmachoi) are built as units in the Allies and Mercenaries category. Dismounted cavalry are an option on each unit (Dismounted, -10 pts, Move 4) and count as Cavalry. Where units appear in the book with different Justinian and Heraclian profiles, the Justinian and Heraclian entries are separate units or carry a composition-dependent cost and characteristics. Combined Formations (archers or javelineers in the rear ranks) are not built as mixed units: archers are separate entries (Skutatoi Archers) that must be combined with Skutatoi.

ARMY COMPOSITIONS (pick one in the Army composition list):
[Early Byzantines - Justinian Dynasty]
  Characters: up to 25%
  Cavalry: up to 50%
  Infantry: up to 50%
  Allies and Mercenaries: up to 33%
  JUSTINIAN DYNASTY (527-582 AD). Characters up to 25%; Cavalry up to 50% (at least two units of bow-armed cavalry must be chosen - not enforced; dismounted cavalry count as cavalry); Infantry up to 50% (Heraclian Regulars may not be chosen); Allies up to 33% (Symmachoi, plus Alans from the Steppe Nomads allies and Early Slavs from the Balkan Bulgars &amp; Slavs list - documented only). Justinian Byzantine armies led by a Magister may use the Stratagem special rule. Up to two Bucellarii models may be upgraded to Doruphoroi (+5 pts), each leading a unit (not built).
[Early Byzantines - Heraclian Dynasty]
  Characters: up to 25%
  Cavalry: up to 75%
  Infantry: up to 50%
  Allies and Mercenaries: up to 25%
  HERACLIAN DYNASTY (582-641 AD; includes Maurice). Characters up to 25%; Cavalry up to 75%; Infantry up to 50% (dismounted cavalrymen count as Infantry); Allies up to 25% on Hun and Ghassanid allies (alternatively up to 25% on Alans and Early Khazars from the Steppe Nomads list - documented only). Heraclian Byzantine armies led by a Magister or Emperor may use the Stratagem special rule.</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
</catalogue>
